; A balancing group that exchanges two commodities without stating a cost
; or leaving a posting blank gets an inferred price.  Ledger normally
; prices the commodity of its first posting in the other.  If that
; posting holds neither residual commodity, as with a zero fee in a third
; commodity, the fallback is the first commodity to enter the balance.
; A zero sum never enters the balance, so in the first transaction the
; zero EUR fee leaves GBP as the first component.  In the second, the
; balanced virtual budget lines form a separate group: GBP is the real
; group's first posting and determines its price direction directly.
; Both transactions put lots on Assets:GBP and infer GBP prices in $ and
; EUR.  The choice must not depend on the balance map's iteration order.
; xact-price-inference-cancel-first.test covers cancelled real transfers;
; 3314_inference_order.test covers the fallback in bracketed groups.

2024/01/05 Exchange with a zero fee first
    Assets:Fee              0 EUR
    Assets:GBP            100 GBP
    Assets:USD           $-130

2024/02/05 Exchange after budget lines
    [Budget:Travel]       $100
    [Budget:Available]   $-100
    Assets:GBP            100 GBP
    Assets:EUR           -115 EUR

test bal --lots --flat --no-total Assets
            -115 EUR  Assets:EUR
    100 GBP {$1.3} [2024/01/05]
100 GBP {1.15 EUR} [2024/02/05]  Assets:GBP
               $-130  Assets:USD
end test

test prices
2024/01/05 GBP              $1.3
2024/02/05 GBP          1.15 EUR
end test
